Hello Coastline Purchasing,

Case TS-5581 opened for this. What you reported: "the scheduled ERP export ... has arrived with a different column order" since Saturday, and Epicor rejects the file on field 7.

Cause: the March 21 release added a header row and two new columns (plant_code, line_id) to scheduled exports. They were inserted at positions 3 and 4 rather than appended at the end, which shifts everything after them for imports that map by position. Nothing on your side caused it.

Fix, about two minutes:
1. Settings > Exports > Scheduled > coastline_orders_daily > Edit
2. Under "Column layout", choose "Legacy (pinned)" and untick "Include header row"
3. Save, then "Run now" to regenerate today's file

The pinned layout keeps the exact column order you had before March 21 and will not change on future releases. I ran a test export against your account and confirmed the output matches the March 20 layout column for column. If you want the new columns later, "Custom" lets you place them at the end.

Please let me know once tonight's import goes through and I will close the case.

Ruth | Tessera Support

